export const GUIDE = "- Tell us about your truck: Tap Truck. Enter how tall, heavy, and long it is. Then we keep you away from low bridges and roads trucks can't use.\n- Pick where to go: Tap here and type an address or a company name. Then tap Start. The phone tells you every turn out loud.\n- Route: your trip: Tap Route to see your way there, how long it takes, tolls and fuel stops. You can save maps here for places with no signal.\n- Faster route: Switch or Keep: If traffic builds up, RigRoute tells you about a faster truck-safe road. Tap Switch to take it or Keep to stay. It never changes your route by itself.\n- HOS: your driving clock: Tap HOS to see how many hours you can still drive today and when your break is due. It is a helper, not your legal log.\n- Load: your job: Tap Load for your pickup, drop-off, times and papers like the BOL. Loads your dispatcher sends you show up here.\n- Warn other drivers: See a crash, police, or road work? Tap here. Other drivers will see it on their map.\n- Me: you and your settings: Tap Me for your points, friends, account, language and voice. Something broken or have an idea? Use Report a Bug / Suggestion there.\n- Help RigRoute grow: In Me you can choose to share your city and state, never your exact spot. It is off unless you turn it on.\n- Report a Bug / Suggestion: In Me, open Report a Bug / Suggestion. Say what went wrong or what to add. You can add a screenshot.\n- Email us: In Me, under Report a Bug, tap Email us to write to the RigRoute team.\n- Need help?: Tap ? on any screen. It tells you what the screen does, and it can read it out loud. You can also type a question or tap Show me around.";
